ir. Reject groups with inconsistent names.\n   e. Identify 'established facts' within the group: entries where polarity is 'positive' or 'negative' (exclude 'unknown').\n   f. Evaluate Policy Logic for each group:\n      i. Check 'all_of': Group passes only if ALL specified (relation, polarity) pairs exist as established facts in the group.\n      ii. Check 'any_of': If the list is non-empty, group passes only if AT LEAST ONE specified pair exists as an established fact. If list is empty, this condition is trivially true.\n      iii. Check 'none_of': Group fails if ANY specified (relation, polarity) pair exists as an established fact in the group.\n      iv. A group must have at least one established fact to be considered valid for fact-checking; if no facts exist, it cannot satisfy non-empty 'all_of' or 'any_of' requirements.\n   g. Filter groups that pass all policy conditions.\n   h. For passing groups, aggregate 'evidence_ids' from established records that match 'all_of' OR 'any_of' criteria. If both 'all_of' and 'any_of' are empty, use evidence_ids from ALL established records in the group.\n   i. Preserve original record order and remove duplicate IDs in the evidence list.\n   j. Construct output entities list preserving group order by first eligible established record. Set unique_entity_count to the number of passing groups.\n5. Final Output: Return JSON {entities: [...], unique_entity_count: int}.\nInvariants: [\"Input validation is strict: non-blank required strings, strict booleans, unique evidence IDs, and exact contiguous quote validation are mandatory in both modes.\", \"Legacy mode behavior is preserved exactly when 'policy' is absent: full union of eligible groups, atomic validation of evidence/entries, and rejection of inconsistent names.\", \"Policy mode enforces name consistency per (scope, group_id) only, not across different scopes.\", \"Only eligible:true records within the exact selected scope are considered for policy evaluation.\", \"Unknown 